# the program hands a built-in to a function of its own. Where that function writes on it the write is followed there, under a key that nobody can read too. Where nobody writes, the members keep their locks
# No operation names what it hands on: only the flow knows that the constructors of the two instances are Date and Map
# put(new Date().constructor, name, f); same(new Map().constructor); Date.now(); Date.parse("0"); Map.groupBy("0", f);
# Date has members that the table locks, and nobody can read the name: the build says so at the store
